  "body": "Almost all HTML parsers are vulnerable to stack overflows and denial-of-service attacks, because HTML parsing can easily be made to exhibit quadratic behavior by deep nesting of documents, and because naive tree-traversal algorithms are recursive.\r\n\r\nI propose that the nesting depth of an HTML document be capped at 500.  Any attempt to insert a node at a depth past that is erroneous — DOM APIs throw exceptions, while an implicit end tag is inserted if this is encountered during parsing.",
